OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGBR TO REFUND PASSENGERS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGFOR POOR SERVICE
OL,4,D
OL,5, British Rail has unveiled plans to
OL,6, refund passengers when trains are late.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FIt has launched its passenger's charter
OL,9,Fwhich sets separate performance targets
OL,10,Ffor different parts of the network.
OL,11,F
OL,12,FInterCity must get 90% of its peak hour
OL,13,Ftrains in on time; parts of Network
OL,14,FSouthEast have been set lower standards
OL,15,F
OL,16,FIf targets are not met, season ticket-
OL,17,Fholders will get discounts of up to 10%
OL,18,Fon renewal. Other passengers will get
OL,19,Fvouchers for 20% of the ticket price if
OL,20,Ftheir trains are over an hour late.
OL,21,F
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG04-03-92
OL,23,D] FMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
