OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLORRY DRIVER SHOT DEAD
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGIN COUNTY ARMAGH
OL,4,D
OL,5, A lorry driver has been shot dead near
OL,6, Tandragee in County Armagh.
OL,8,FJames Grey, 39, who started work for
OL,9,Fthe quarry firm on Monday, was thought
OL,10,Fto be a Roman Catholic. He was shot in
OL,11,Fhis lorry cab on Markethill Road.
OL,13,FHe was understood to have been taking
OL,14,Fa load of sand or stones to a private
OL,15,Fdevelopment at Portadown - not a police
OL,16,Fstation as earlier reported.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FMr Grey, of Fairgreen, Keady, married
OL,19,Fwith five children, was the 32nd person
OL,20,Fkilled in paramilitary violence in
OL,21,FNorthern Ireland this year.
OL,23,D]FFromG04-03-92F/ teletextarchive.com
